# Git commit and PR attribution

- Never add a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer naming Cursor, Claude, Copilot,
  Codex, ChatGPT, Gemini, or any other AI assistant to a commit message or
  PR description.
- Never add "Generated with Cursor", "AI-assisted", "AI-generated",
  session-link footers, or any other AI attribution, logo, or metadata to a
  commit message, PR title, PR description, or PR comment.
- Commits and PRs must read as 100% authored by the human user. Do not
  mention AI involvement anywhere in commit/PR content.

<!--
  Also disable Cursor's built-in commit-message co-author behavior in
  Settings > Features > Commit Message (or the equivalent in newer
  versions: Settings > Rules / Cursor Settings > Git) if such a toggle is
  present in your installed version — the setting name has moved between
  releases, so check the current Cursor settings UI rather than relying on
  a fixed path. This file's rule + the commit-msg hook are the durable
  backstop either way.
-->
